# Kasimir Velikov, the dusk elf who lodges with the Vistani outside Vallaki (docs/voice/kasimir_velikov.md).
# The Tarokka can name him as the party's ally (the Seer).

~ start
if not flag.kasimir_met
set kasimir_met
Narrator: Away from the fire, on a stool by a wagon with its shutters closed, sits an elf with ash-dark skin and white hair, mending a net he will never cast. He doesn't look up until you are close enough to touch.
Kasimir: The strangers. The camp talks of nothing else. Sit, if you like. I am poor company. I have been poor company for a very long time.
else
Kasimir: Back again, to the saddest wagon in the camp. People will start to talk.
endif
-> menu

~ menu
* Who are you? -> who
* Why do the Vistani shelter an elf? -> vistani
* [Insight DC 13] What is he grieving for? -> grief_ok | grief_fail
* [if not flag.kasimir_sister_told] (Sit with him a while, and say nothing.) -> sit
* [if flag.kasimir_sister_told] Tell us about the temple in the mountains. -> temple
* [if tarokka.ally.npc == kasimir_velikov and not guest:kasimir_velikov] Madam Eva's cards named you as our ally. -> ally
* [name:wren_featherfoot] [if quest.the_last_lesson and not flag.wren_letter_given] Give him Master Sorrel's letter. -> companions/lesson:kasimir
* We heard you have spells to spare. Scrolls? -> scrolls
* Goodbye. -> bye

~ who
Kasimir: Kasimir Velikov. My people came to this valley long ago, the elves of the dusk, as guests of its lord. We stayed as his tenants. Now there are only a handful of us, none of us young, and there will never be another. That was his doing. And, I am afraid, a little of ours.
interject species:elf: I have heard songs about the dusk elves. None of them end like that.
Kasimir: The songs were written before the ending. They usually are.
interject name:wren_featherfoot: Kasimir. Sir. I... no. Not yet. Sorry. Please, go on.
-> menu

~ vistani
Kasimir: Long ago a Vistana I had never met fell sick with a fever on the road, and I sat with her three nights until it broke. Her grandchildren still bring me soup. The Vistani forget nothing: not a kindness, not an insult.
if flag.tser_pool_brawl_won
Kasimir: Which is why, if I were you, I would not linger by their fire. They have heard what happened at Tser Pool.
endif
-> menu

~ grief_ok
Narrator: Grief, yes, but older and sharper than grief: the kind of guilt that has had centuries to settle into the bones.
-> grief_told

~ sit
time +60
Narrator: You sit. He mends. The camp's fire burns down and is built up again, and nobody says anything for a long while, which seems to be the point.
Kasimir: You are patient. The young rarely are. Very well; you have paid for it.
approve wren_featherfoot +2 liriel_dawnsong +1: You sat with Kasimir and said nothing
-> grief_told

~ grief_told
set kasimir_sister_told
Kasimir: My sister, Patrina. Cleverer than me, prouder than me. She went up to the castle of her own will, to learn what its lord knew. Our own people stoned her for it, and I stood at the back and did not stop them.
Kasimir: Her bones lie under his castle now. They say there is a temple high in the mountains, sealed in amber, where death itself can be argued with. One day I will go there and argue.
interject class:cleric: Some doors are shut for a reason.
Kasimir: I know. I have stood behind one for a very long time.
-> menu

~ grief_fail
Narrator: He looks at the net in his hands, and his hands keep working. Whatever he is mourning, he has worn it smooth.
-> menu

~ temple
Kasimir: Beyond the pass to the north, in the ice. I have read of it, and dreamed of it, and been too much of a coward to climb to it. If ever you go that way, I would like very much to go with you.
-> menu

~ ally
Kasimir: Eva named me? Then the cards have a sense of humour, or a sense of justice. I have never been able to tell those apart.
Kasimir: I will come. Somewhere along your road is the castle, and beneath it, my sister. And past it, perhaps, the temple. It is time I stopped mending nets.
join kasimir_velikov
quest find_the_ally found
-> END

~ scrolls
Kasimir: I write them out at night, when I can't sleep, which is every night. Lesser spells; the ones that matter I keep. Take what you can pay for. Gold buys passage, and I have a long way to go.
shop
-> menu

~ bye
Kasimir: Walk in the light while there is any. It goes quickly here.
-> END
